{"id":"gifts-by-department","title":"Which departments report the most gifts","question":"How much in gifts did each department report on its monthly cover pages, and who was the largest organization giving?","finding":"387 cover pages from 36 departments (2024-11 to 2026-11) report 2,463 gifts valued at $41.9 million on original filings and $1.8 million more on 49 amendments. The largest: Police (POL) $15.3 million, Recreation and Parks (REC) $8.2 million, Mayor's Office (MYR) $7.7 million. 9 cover pages ($365,513) are new since the download of 12 November and are not yet in the itemised list on disk, which ends 2026-10-31.","how":"Sums of the \"total number of gifts\" and \"total gift value\" printed on each cover page in the export saved on 17 November 2026, by the department named on it. Amendments are summed apart because a cover page does not say whether an amendment restates or adds to the original. The largest organization gift is read from the itemised list joined to the cover page by envelope number; individual donors are never named.","limits":"Gifts to departments are permitted and mostly go to public programmes; a large total is a measure of generosity and of what the department chose to report, not of influence. Some gifts are grants from other governments or foundations accepted by ordinance. Departments that file nothing in a month may have received nothing. If an amendment restates its original, the two columns overlap.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"dept","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"value","t":"Gift value, original filings","type":"usd"},{"k":"gifts","t":"Gifts","type":"int"},{"k":"amendValue","t":"Value on amendments","type":"usd"},{"k":"amendGifts","t":"Gifts on amendments","type":"int"},{"k":"months","t":"Months with a cover page","type":"int"},{"k":"covers","t":"Cover pages","type":"int"},{"k":"newValue","t":"On cover pages new since 12 Nov","type":"usd"},{"k":"largestOrgGift","t":"Largest single gift from an organization","type"